{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Valid-predicated load-use interlock\n\nChanged:\n- Replaced IF-stage NOP-word injection with raw imem forwarding plus the existing valid bit.\n- Added decoder `uses_rs1` / `uses_rs2` predicates and used them in `hazard_unit` so load-use stalls only compare architecturally live sources on valid IF/ID work.\n- ID now captures a zero bubble whenever it accepts an invalid fetch.\n- Carried source-use metadata through the pipe for RVFI data selection.\n- Added RVFI-only raw regfile read ports so unused raw RVFI source fields match the cosim contract without reintroducing execution stalls.\n- Added focused `test_hazard.py` coverage for true hazards, immediate-bit false hazards, and invalid IF/ID work.\n\nDeviations:\n- RVFI source addresses remain raw instruction fields to match the existing Python ISS/cosim contract. Source-use predicates only choose whether RVFI source data comes from the executed operand path or an RVFI-only raw regfile read.\n\nConcerns:\n- The RVFI raw read ports are verification-facing and should be pruned from timed FPGA logic because they only feed RVFI outputs. They are not used by execute or hazard decisions.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Cocotb bench tests: pass (`pytest -q cores/bench/test`).\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`).\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1` (`make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
