{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"Registered IF/ID control boundary implementation.\n\nChanged rtl/if_stage.sv from a combinational IF/ID output to a clocked IF/ID\nregister alongside the PC register. Redirect still updates PC immediately;\nIF/ID valid is cleared on redirect, held on downstream stalls, and loaded as a\nbubble on imem stalls when decode is free to advance.\n\nChanged rtl/hazard_unit.sv to target the registered boundary. Load-use checks\nnow use IF/ID.valid plus registered rs fields. imem stalls hold PC but do not\nhold IF/ID unless there is also a downstream stall. dmem stalls and DIV/REM\nbusy still hold IF/ID and ID/EX; load-use and redirect still bubble ID/EX when\nEX/MEM can accept progress.\n\nChanged rtl/core.sv wiring to carry separate PC stall, IF/ID hold/flush, and\nID/EX hold/flush controls. core_pkg.sv comment updated to describe IF/ID as a\nregistered payload. No top-level IO or RVFI channel contract changes.\n\nDeviation: I kept the existing hazard_unit naming for stall_if/flush_if at the\ntop level, adding hold_if_id instead of a larger control-bus rewrite. This keeps\nthe change small while still breaking the combinational imem/redirect-to-decode\npath.\n\nConcerns: The registered IF/ID stage adds an extra fetch/decode fill and\nredirect bubble versus the previous combinational IF/ID behavior. Throughput is\nstill one instruction per cycle after fill.\n\nLocal checks:\n- Verilator lint: pass with `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed with `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n- Cosim: plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` built the harness with default\n  `NRET=2` and failed before simulation because this core declares `nret: 1`.\n  Rerun with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
