{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Fall-through fetch prebuffer implementation notes\n\nWhat changed:\n- Replaced the IF stage's tightly coupled PC/imem handoff with a 4-entry\n  fall-through prefetch FIFO.\n- Added direct empty-FIFO bypass from a ready imem word into decode so the\n  zero-wait path does not gain a fixed extra cycle.\n- Redirects flush the FIFO and restart the fetch PC at the redirect target.\n- Hazard control now treats backend stalls as \"do not dequeue into decode\";\n  the IF stage can keep fetching while dmem stalls, DIV/REM busy, or load-use\n  bubbles hold the backend.\n- Added a compact fetch entry typedef in core_pkg.sv. The IF implementation\n  uses parallel arrays for Yosys compatibility.\n\nDeviations:\n- No new cocotb test was added in this pass. The change is covered locally by\n  lint, riscv-formal, and cosim.\n- The FIFO storage was flattened instead of using an array-of-struct writes\n  because Yosys rejected variable-index struct field assignment syntax.\n\nConcerns:\n- The queue adds a small amount of frontend state and muxing. Timing impact\n  should be checked by the Gowin flow.\n\nLocal verification:\n- PASS: verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv\n- PASS: RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh\n  Result: 53 passed, 0 failed.\n- PASS: NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench\n  Result: {\"passed\": true, \"elfs_tested\": 2}\n- Note: plain make cosim TARGET=bench built the harness with default NRET=2 in\n  this checkout and failed before simulation by looking for non-existent _1\n  RVFI ports on the nret=1 core.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented the fall-through fetch prebuffer in `cores/bench/rtl`:\n\n- `if_stage.sv`: 4-entry fetch FIFO, empty-queue bypass, redirect flush, independent fetch PC.\n- `hazard_unit.sv`: backend stalls now stop FIFO dequeue, not frontend fetch.\n- `core.sv` / `core_pkg.sv`: wiring and compact fetch metadata.\n\nVerification:\n- `verilator --lint-only ...`: pass\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53/53\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, selftest + CoreMark\n\nNotes written to `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`."}}
