{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Cold high-multiply sidecar\n\nWhat changed:\n- Kept low-half MUL in rtl/alu.sv and removed real MULH/MULHU/MULHSU products\n  from the non-ALTOPS hot ALU path.\n- Added rtl/mulh_unit.sv, an iterative 32-cycle shift/add high-half multiplier\n  for MULH, MULHU, and MULHSU.\n- Wired mulh_unit into rtl/ex_stage.sv with the existing EX busy/start/done/\n  accept pattern used by div_unit.sv. The pipeline injects bubbles while the\n  sidecar runs, then retires the held instruction with latched source operands.\n- Updated tests so test_alu.py covers only hot low-half MUL, added\n  test_mulh_unit.py for the sidecar arithmetic, and added a pipeline test that\n  forwards a MULH result into a dependent ADD.\n\nDeviations:\n- I did not change hazard_unit.sv or core.sv. The existing ex_busy signal was\n  already generic enough for DIV/REM and now also covers MULH*.\n- The sidecar is a simple 32-cycle unit rather than a shorter partial-product\n  implementation. This minimizes new combinational multiplier logic on timed\n  paths.\n\nConcerns:\n- MULH/MULHU/MULHSU now take roughly the same class of stall as DIV/REM, so a\n  workload with frequent high-half multiplies will lose IPC. The hypothesis\n  assumes these ops are cold for CoreMark.\n- Plain `make cosim TARGET=bench` in this checkout invokes build.sh without\n  passing NRET from core.yaml, so it tries to build the nret=1 core as NRET=2.\n  The orchestrator path and `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` use the correct\n  nret=1 contract.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Focused cocotb tests: pass (`test_alu.py`, `test_mulh_unit.py`,\n  `test_pipeline.py`).\n- Formal: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench\n  bash formal/run_all.sh`).\n- Cosim: `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
