{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/rtl/loop_predictor.sv\"","aggregated_output":"// rtl/loop_predictor.sv\n//\n// One-entry backward-branch target predictor with a single outstanding\n// prediction scoreboard. The predictor table is a full-PC tag, an aligned\n// target, and a 2-bit saturating counter. IF may use the table only while no\n// prediction is outstanding; EX resolves the outstanding record by PC and\n// trains the table from conditional branches.\nmodule loop_predictor (\n  input  logic        clock,\n  input  logic        reset,\n\n  // IF lookup. A hit means \"fetch this PC's instruction, but set next PC to\n  // lookup_target\"; no prediction metadata is carried in the pipeline.\n  input  logic [31:0] lookup_pc,\n  output logic        lookup_hit,\n  output logic [31:0] lookup_target,\n\n  // IF accepted a predicted fetch this cycle.\n  input  logic        predict_fire,\n  input  logic [31:0] predict_pc,\n  input  logic [31:0] predict_target,\n\n  // EX accepted the instruction corresponding to the outstanding record.\n  input  logic        resolve_valid,\n\n  // Conditional-branch training from EX.\n  input  logic        train_valid,\n  input  logic [31:0] train_pc,\n  input  logic        train_taken,\n  input  logic        train_backward,\n  input  logic [31:0] train_target,\n\n  // Outstanding record visible to EX for next-PC verification.\n  output logic        outstanding_valid,\n  output logic [31:0] outstanding_pc,\n  output logic [31:0] outstanding_target\n);\n\n  logic        entry_valid_q;\n  logic [31:0] entry_pc_q;\n  logic [31:0] entry_target_q;\n  logic [1:0]  entry_ctr_q;\n\n  logic        out_valid_q;\n  logic [31:0] out_pc_q;\n  logic [31:0] out_target_q;\n\n  wire [31:0] aligned_train_target   = train_target & 32'hffff_fffc;\n  wire [31:0] aligned_predict_target = predict_target & 32'hffff_fffc;\n\n  assign lookup_hit = entry_valid_q\n                   && !out_valid_q\n                   && entry_ctr_q[1]\n                   && (entry_pc_q == lookup_pc);\n  assign lookup_target = entry_target_q;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (reset) begin\n      entry_valid_q  <= 1'b0;\n      entry_pc_q     <= 32'b0;\n      entry_target_q <= 32'b0;\n      entry_ctr_q    <= 2'b00;\n      out_valid_q    <= 1'b0;\n      out_pc_q       <= 32'b0;\n      out_target_q   <= 32'b0;\n    end else begin\n      if (train_valid) begin\n        if (train_taken && train_backward) begin\n          if (entry_valid_q\n              && entry_pc_q == train_pc\n              && entry_target_q == aligned_train_target) begin\n            if (entry_ctr_q != 2'b11) begin\n              entry_ctr_q <= entry_ctr_q + 2'b01;\n            end\n          end else begin\n            entry_valid_q  <= 1'b1;\n            entry_pc_q     <= train_pc;\n            entry_target_q <= aligned_train_target;\n            entry_ctr_q    <= 2'b10;  // weakly taken, predicts on next visit\n          end\n        end else if (entry_valid_q && entry_pc_q == train_pc) begin\n          if (entry_ctr_q != 2'b00) begin\n            entry_ctr_q <= entry_ctr_q - 2'b01;\n          end\n        end\n      end\n\n      if (resolve_valid) begin\n        out_valid_q <= 1'b0;\n      end\n      if (predict_fire) begin\n        out_valid_q  <= 1'b1;\n        out_pc_q     <= predict_pc;\n        out_target_q <= aligned_predict_target;\n      end\n    end\n  end\n\n  assign outstanding_valid  = out_valid_q;\n  assign outstanding_pc     = out_pc_q;\n  assign outstanding_target = out_target_q;\n\nendmodule\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"ls cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n## Outstanding Loop Target Predictor\n\nChanged the bench core from an always-redirect-on-taken-control-flow policy to\na one-entry backward-branch predictor with one global outstanding prediction\nrecord.\n\nActual changes:\n- Added `rtl/loop_predictor.sv`, containing a full-PC tag, aligned target,\n  2-bit saturating counter, and `{valid, pc, target}` outstanding scoreboard.\n- `if_stage.sv` now uses a predictor hit as the next PC, but does not add any\n  prediction fields to the IF/ID payload.\n- `ex_stage.sv` recomputes the resolved architectural next PC, compares it\n  against the outstanding record, suppresses redirects on matches, redirects to\n  the resolved PC on mismatches, and emits branch train/resolve sideband events.\n- `core.sv` wires lookup, accepted-prediction fire, outstanding verification,\n  and training. Prediction fire is gated by fetch acceptance so imem stalls,\n  redirects, and pipeline stalls do not allocate stale outstanding records.\n- Added `test/test_loop_predictor.py` for predictor reset, training, scoreboard\n  suppression, resolve clear, target alignment, and loop-exit counter decay.\n  Updated `test/test_pipeline.py`'s explicit core source list to include the new\n  RTL file.\n\nDeviations:\n- I decrement the counter on any resolved conditional branch at the stored tag\n  that is not a taken backward branch. This keeps loop exits and stale/reused\n  branch PCs from staying permanently confident.\n- Training is committed only when EX is not held by a dmem stall; redirect\n  recovery may still assert during the stall so the PC can be driven to the\n  recovery target while the outstanding record remains available for repeated\n  comparison.\n\nConcerns:\n- The predictor adds a 32-bit lookup comparator and target mux on the fetch PC\n  update path. The intended savings are reduced control bubbles; FPGA timing\n  will decide whether the added lookup is cheap enough on this device.\n- The predictor intentionally allows a saturated loop branch to remain\n  confident after a single exit decrement, so hot loops should keep predicting\n  across repeated invocations.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_loop_predictor.py`: pass\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: pass\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass\n  (`Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed`)\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench`: failed because the local Makefile invocation left\n  `NRET` at the cosim harness default of 2 while this core declares `nret: 1`;\n  this makes `main.cpp` look for nonexistent `_1` RVFI ports.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1`: pass (`passed: true`, 2 ELFs tested)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
