{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Carry-select hot ALU adder\n\nWhat changed:\n- Replaced ALU ADD and SUB result generation in `rtl/alu.sv` with explicit four-block 8-bit carry-select datapaths.\n- Kept the existing ALU opcode case, M-extension sidecar behavior, forwarding, memory effective-address lane, branch comparator, and writeback mux unchanged.\n- Reused the carry-select ADD/SUB results for the RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS M-extension substitute formulas so formal arithmetic behavior stays identical.\n- Strengthened `test/test_alu.py` ADD/SUB vectors around byte-block carry boundaries, wraparound, signed-overflow-looking cases, and subtraction borrow chains.\n\nDeviations:\n- Implemented separate ADD and SUB carry-select datapaths instead of a single shared adder/subtractor. This avoids putting the ADD/SUB opcode-controlled invert/carry mux directly in front of the block adders, at the cost of extra LUT area.\n\nConcerns:\n- The change trades area for timing as intended. Whether Gowin maps the 8-bit precompute blocks and carry muxes into a faster route than the previous 32-bit carry chain needs vendor timing to confirm.\n- The load/store effective-address adder remains the existing flat `rs1 + imm` side lane per the hypothesis, so memory-address timing is intentionally unchanged.\n\nLocal checks:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `python3 -m pytest cores/bench/test/test_alu.py`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed and 0 failed.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench`: failed to build because the standalone Makefile defaulted the cosim C++ harness to `NRET=2` while `cores/bench/core.yaml` declares `nret: 1`.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
