{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_62","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Source-aware EX operand mux slimming\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added id_ex_uses_rs1/id_ex_uses_rs2 inputs to rtl/forward_unit.sv and gated\n  EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding selects with those decoded source-live bits.\n- Wired id_ex_w.uses_rs1/id_ex_w.uses_rs2 into the forward unit from rtl/core.sv.\n- Changed rtl/id_stage.sv so AUIPC latches the instruction PC into the\n  execution rs1_val copy while keeping uses_rs1 false for architectural/RVFI\n  source semantics.\n- Removed the AUIPC-specific ALU A mux in rtl/ex_stage.sv; ALU A now consumes\n  the forwarded rs1 value directly.\n- Added focused cocotb coverage:\n  - test_forward_unit.py checks live-source forwarding, EX/MEM priority,\n    MEM/WB forwarding, x0 suppression, and unused-source alias suppression.\n  - test_pipeline.py adds an AUIPC case whose immediate bits alias a just-written\n    rs1 field, then checks AUIPC still uses pc+imm and the following ADDI still\n    forwards the AUIPC result.\n\nDeviations:\n- Did not zero unused source addresses in ID/EX. Keeping the raw instruction\n  fields preserves existing RVFI source reporting behavior and avoids widening\n  the change.\n\nConcerns:\n- None known in the RTL. The bare `make cosim TARGET=bench` invocation defaults\n  the harness to NRET=2 and fails to compile against this nret=1 core; rerunning\n  with NRET=1 matches cores/bench/core.yaml and passes.\n\nLocal checks:\n- verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl\n  cores/bench/rtl/*.sv: pass.\n- RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh: pass\n  (53 passed, 0 failed).\n- NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench: pass (2 ELFs tested).\n- PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider\n  cores/bench/test/test_forward_unit.py cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py: pass.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
