{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"I’m making that cleanup: LOAD/STORE decoder arms will drive a pass-immediate ALU op, while the real byte address comes only from `eff_addr`. That avoids adding a memory-op select term to the EX writeback-result mux and better matches the hypothesis’ “separate lane, no new priority mux” intent."}}
