{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"EX now distinguishes the architectural redirect from a prediction repair: if a predicted branch or direct JAL resolves to the stored target, it suppresses the flush; if it resolves not-taken or to another target, it redirects to the architectural next PC. Training is gated to the cycle where EX actually advances, so dmem stalls don’t accidentally age the table multiple times."}}
