{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_77","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"ID link-register JALR predictor\n\nWhat changed:\n- Added a one-bit `predicted_jalr` tag to the ID/EX payload.\n- Added exact x1/x5 shadow registers in `core.sv`, updated only from the WB\n  write stream and bypassed with same-cycle WB data.\n- Added dirty detection for unresolved x1/x5 writers in ID/EX and EX/MEM.\n- Added ID-stage detection for legal, valid, un-stalled JALR through x1/x5.\n  Clean, aligned targets redirect fetch early via `(link_value + imm) & ~1`.\n- Added an ID redirect input to `if_stage`, with EX redirect priority above it.\n- Suppressed EX's redundant JALR redirect only for tagged, non-trapping JALR.\n\nDeviations:\n- For predicted JALR, ID/EX `rs1_val` is loaded from the same clean link shadow\n  used for the early redirect. This keeps EX `pc_next` and IF's early PC update\n  on the same value without carrying a predicted target, and made the pc_fwd\n  formal proof tractable. Non-predicted JALR and all other instructions still\n  use the normal regfile read path.\n- No cocotb test was added; the riscv-formal JALR/pc_fwd checks and full cosim\n  were used as the local guards for this iteration.\n\nConcerns:\n- The predictor adds a small ID-stage add/align path into the PC update. It is\n  intentionally limited to x1/x5 JALR and avoids fetch-time tables or EX target\n  comparison, but timing should still be reviewed in the Gowin flow.\n- Dirty blocking is conservative for all ID/EX and EX/MEM writers to x1/x5,\n  even if the value could be forwarded.\n\nLocal status:\n- Verilator lint: pass.\n- Formal: pass on attempt 2 (`53 passed, 0 failed`). Attempt 1 was stopped\n  after `pc_fwd_ch0` spent over five minutes in the solver; using the same\n  shadow value for predicted ID/EX `rs1_val` resolved that.\n- Cosim: pass with `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` (`2` ELFs tested). Plain\n  `make cosim TARGET=bench` built the harness with default `NRET=2` and failed\n  before simulation because this core exposes the single-channel RVFI port set.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
