{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"test -f cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,120p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && git status --short --ignored cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Tiny return-address predictor implementation notes\n\nChanged:\n- Added a `predicted_return` bit to IF/ID and ID/EX.\n- Added `rtl/return_predictor.sv`: 4-entry RAS, 4 learned return-PC tags, and one outstanding predicted target record.\n- IF consults the return predictor using the current fetch PC and redirects to the RAS top only on a learned return-PC hit with no outstanding prediction.\n- EX classifies link-register calls and return-style JALR instructions, trains/pushes/pops the predictor, and suppresses the normal JALR redirect when a predicted return target matches the resolved next PC.\n- EX redirects to the resolved next PC on return-prediction mismatch or stale learned-PC hits, so recovery uses the existing flush path.\n- Added focused cocotb coverage for predictor reset/default-not-predict, call push/LIFO behavior, repeated return prediction, mismatch recovery, and stalled fetch lookup gating.\n\nDeviations:\n- The RAS speculatively pops on prediction. On mismatch or if an older redirect squashes the outstanding prediction, the RAS is cleared instead of repaired. This is conservative for correctness and avoids extra recovery bookkeeping.\n- The return-PC filter uses full aligned PC tags rather than partial tags, to avoid avoidable alias traffic.\n\nConcerns:\n- The IF path now has a small tag compare and RAS-target mux. This is intentionally much smaller than a general branch target predictor, but timing should still be checked by the Gowin flow.\n- The local `make cosim TARGET=bench` target defaults the harness to `NRET=2`; for this `nret: 1` core I ran it with `NRET=1`, matching `tools.eval.cosim` behavior.\n\nLocal status:\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP -sv +incdir+cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/rtl/*.sv`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_return_predictor.py`: pass.\n- `pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: pass.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`: pass, 53 passed / 0 failed.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: pass, 2 ELFs tested.\n!! cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
