{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"The failure is the expected stale-target corner under formal’s symbolic instruction stream: IF can use an old exact-PC target, then EX sees a taken direct control instruction at the same PC with a different immediate. With only a one-bit marker, suppressing unconditionally breaks `pc_next -> next pc`. I’m going to make EX re-check the predictor target by PC and only suppress when the current resolved target still matches."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"A cleaner fix is to screen the hit in IF against the current instruction’s direct-control immediate. That keeps the pipeline metadata to one bit, rejects stale same-PC/different-target entries before they redirect fetch, and leaves EX’s recovery path for loop exits and non-direct stale hits."}}
