\n- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-001-r12s0 (regression, -5.83%): Moving RV32I shifts into a registered EX sidecar regressed because CoreMark's shift stalls plus new `ex_busy`/result-priority and RVFI source-capture muxing outweighed removing the barrel shifter from the ALU cone, so shifts are not cold enough to serialize.\n- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-002-r12s1 (regression, -16.53%): Extending the registered EX sidecar to SLT/SLTU as well as shifts regressed harder because CoreMark-visible compares now pay extra stalls while `shift_cmp` result-priority, `ex_busy`, and RVFI source-capture muxing still sit on the EX/MEM path.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
