{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-001-r2s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Valid-predicated load-use interlock\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  After moving DIV/REM out of the single-cycle ALU, the best timing report no\n  longer points at arithmetic. The new worst path runs from the register file\n  through ID/EX, EX redirect/fetch control, hazard control, and back into the\n  ID/EX register enable/data mux. The current fetch path also injects a wide\n  NOP instruction on redirect or imem stall, and the load-use interlock\n  compares both raw instruction source fields even when rs2 is actually an\n  immediate bitfield. That is a good micro-optimization target because it is\n  on the hot control path and can create false CoreMark bubbles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace redirect/imem-stall NOP injection with valid-bit bubble handling in\n  ID, and make the load-use interlock source-aware. Fetch should pass the raw\n  imem word plus a valid bit; ID should zero the ID/EX bundle whenever it\n  captures an invalid fetch. The decoder should provide compact uses_rs1 and\n  uses_rs2 predicates, and hazard_unit should compare a load destination only\n  against architecturally live source operands while also ignoring invalid\n  IF/ID work. This removes the EX redirect -> IF instruction mux -> decode /\n  hazard dependency from the ID/EX control path and avoids false stalls on\n  immediate instructions whose imm[4:0] happens to match a preceding load rd.\n  The existing one-cycle true load-use interlock, dmem hold behavior, DIV/REM\n  busy stall, and nret=1 RVFI contract remain unchanged.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact decoded source-use predicate fields to the relevant pipeline bundle so hazard logic can distinguish real register operands from immediate bits.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Expose whether rs1 and rs2 are architecturally consumed by each decoded instruction while keeping illegal-instruction defaults intact.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Stop muxing a full NOP word onto the fetch instruction for redirect/imem bubbles; instead forward the raw imem word and rely on the valid bit.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"When not stalled, capture a zero bubble for invalid fetches and latch the new source-use predicates for valid decoded instructions.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use IF/ID valid plus uses_rs1/uses_rs2 predicates so load-use detection only compares live operands and no longer depends on redirect-driven NOP bits.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the predicate signals through the existing single-issue pipeline without changing the top-level interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_hazard.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage that true load-use hazards still stall once while immediate instructions with matching imm[4:0] do not spuriously stall.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
