{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r2s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r2s1\ntitle: \"Registered IF/ID control boundary\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  After the iterative divider improvement, the timed critical path is no\n  longer dominated by RV32M arithmetic. The reported worst path now loops\n  through decode, execute redirect generation, fetch flush selection, the\n  hazard unit, and back into the ID/EX register enable/data mux. The current\n  IF/ID payload is combinational, so branch redirect, imem stall, load-use\n  detection, and ID/EX capture all sit in one broad control cone.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a real IF/ID pipeline register and restructure stall/flush handling so\n  decode consumes a stable registered instruction instead of the same-cycle\n  imem_data/redirect mux output. The PC should still update immediately on an\n  EX redirect, but wrong-path instructions are killed by clearing the IF/ID\n  valid bit and ID/EX valid bit at their stage boundaries. Hazard detection\n  should use the registered IF/ID rs fields, with IF/ID held on downstream\n  stalls and loaded with a bubble when imem is not ready. This breaks the\n  current combinational redirect-to-fetch-to-hazard-to-ID feedback path while\n  keeping one instruction per cycle throughput after fill and preserving the\n  existing load-use, dmem stall, DIV/REM busy, and RVFI retirement behavior.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Keep or extend the IF/ID bundle as a true registered stage payload with pc, instr, and valid fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace the combinational IF/ID output with a clocked IF/ID register that holds on downstream stalls, bubbles on imem stalls, and clears valid on redirects.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the registered IF/ID payload and simplify ID/EX capture so flush/stall decisions no longer depend on a same-cycle fetch mux output.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Retarget load-use, imem, dmem, EX-busy, and redirect controls to the registered IF/ID boundary and avoid combinational feedback through fetch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire separate IF/ID hold/flush and ID/EX hold/flush controls without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
