{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r3s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-002-r3s1\ntitle: \"Decoupled fetch prebuffer\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current frontend is tightly coupled to decode: an imemReady bubble makes\n  IF/ID invalid immediately, and a dmem stall also holds the PC so the otherwise\n  independent instruction bus cannot fetch ahead. With the benchmark's random\n  22% instruction stalls and separate instruction/data buses, CoreMark is likely\n  losing cycles that could be hidden by fetching sequential instructions during\n  backend stalls and replaying them through later imem bubbles.\nhypothesis: |\n  Replace the combinational IF/ID fetch handoff with a small sequential\n  prefetch FIFO, sized around four entries, that fetches ahead on io_imemReady\n  whenever there is space and supplies decode from its head. The PC generator\n  remains simple and sequential, with EX redirects flushing the FIFO and\n  restarting fetch at the redirect target; no imem_data decode, BTB, or\n  prediction logic is added to the PC update path. This structural decoupling\n  should improve iterations per cycle by allowing fetch to run during dmem\n  stalls, DIV/REM busy periods, and load-use bubbles, then absorb short random\n  imemReady gaps without increasing the existing EX ALU critical path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact fetch queue entry type or metadata fields for prefetched pc, instr, and valid state if needed by the frontend.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Turn the IF stage into a small sequential prefetch FIFO with head dequeue to decode, tail enqueue from imemReady, redirect flush, and simple sequential fetch PC management.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Separate backend decode-consume stalls from frontend fetch-advance permission so imem can continue filling the FIFO while dmem or EX busy holds decode.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consume the FIFO head valid bit exactly like the current IF/ID valid bubble semantics, preserving existing invalid-fetch-to-bubble behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the new fetch dequeue/space controls into the existing single-issue pipeline without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_fetch_fifo.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for imem stall hiding, dmem-stall fetch-ahead, redirect FIFO flush, and no duplicate or skipped retirement order.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
