{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"ls -l cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r4s1.yaml && sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r4s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"-rw-rw----+ 1 hwebench3 hwebench3 2527 Oct  3 23:29 cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-002-r4s1.yaml\nid: hyp-20261003-002-r4s1\ntitle: \"Cold high-multiply sidecar\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current best core has already removed DIV/REM from the hot ALU path, but\n  the remaining critical path still runs through the EX operand/ALU/result cone.\n  A prior structural attempt regressed because it made every RV32M multiply\n  multicycle, and CoreMark uses ordinary low-half MUL in hot loops. The colder\n  high-half multiply operations still drag extra signed/unsigned 64-bit product\n  logic and result muxing into the single-cycle ALU despite being unlikely in\n  CoreMark's C workload.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the execute structure into a hot one-cycle lane for RV32I operations\n  plus low-half MUL, and a cold multicycle sidecar for MULH, MULHU, MULHSU,\n  DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU. The existing iterative DIV/REM stall protocol can\n  be extended so high-half multiply starts a small signedness-aware multicycle\n  unit while fetch/decode are held exactly like current division. Under\n  RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, keep the current combinational substitute formulas so\n  fast formal remains tractable. This should shrink the hot ALU's multiplier\n  and result-select structure without adding cycles to the CoreMark MUL-heavy\n  path, offering an Fmax gain with little IPC risk.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Keep RV32I and low-half MUL in the one-cycle ALU, but remove real MULH/MULHU/MULHSU hardware from the hot non-ALTOPS result path while preserving ALTOPS substitutes.\"\n  - file: rtl/mulh_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a small multicycle high-half multiply sidecar that handles signed, unsigned, and signed-by-unsigned high-product results with RV32M-correct edge behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Route MULH/MULHU/MULHSU through the sidecar using the existing EX busy/accept pattern, while leaving low-half MUL and ordinary ALU operations single-cycle.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Reuse or generalize the existing EX busy stall so high-half multiply holds IF/ID and ID/EX with the same ordering guarantees as DIV/REM.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire any generalized M-sidecar busy/result signals through the current single-issue pipeline without changing the top-level IO or nret=1 RVFI contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Adjust M-extension unit tests so low-half MUL remains covered in the ALU and high-half multiply results are checked through the new sidecar path.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
