Refactor execute into EX1 operand/branch logic plus EX2 ALU/address/result logic, preserving the existing DIV/REM and MULH sidecar accept protocol.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Extend bypass selection for the split execute pipeline, including EX2-to-EX1 and MEM/WB-to-EX1 paths with x0 suppression.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Adjust interlocks for the extra execute register so load-use, sidecar-busy, dmem-stall, and redirect flush behavior remain in-order and single-retire.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the split execute stage and revised forwarding/stall signals without changing the top-level IO or nret=1 RVFI port contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_hazard.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage for ALU-to-ALU forwarding through EX2-to-EX1, branch-after-ALU dependencies, load-use stalls, and dmem-stall ordering.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
