{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r1s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Static direct-control-flow predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The current five-stage core resolves every branch and jump in EX, then flushes\n  the younger IF and ID work on any taken redirect. CoreMark has many loop-back\n  branches and direct calls/jumps, so paying the full redirect penalty on every\n  taken direct control-flow instruction leaves meaningful iterations/cycle on\n  the table even if Fmax is unchanged. A very small predictor should improve IPC\n  without touching the existing critical ALU/forwarding path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a decode-time static predictor in fetch for direct control flow: predict\n  JAL as taken to its immediate target and predict conditional branches with a\n  backward offset as taken while leaving forward branches and all JALR/returns\n  predicted not-taken. Carry predicted_taken and predicted_target with the\n  instruction into EX, where the already-existing branch/jump resolution compares\n  actual next PC against the predicted next PC and redirects only on mismatch.\n  Correctly predicted backward loop branches and direct JALs should retire with\n  no redirect bubbles; only loop exits, forward taken branches, JALR, and\n  mispredictions pay the current recovery cost.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted_taken and predicted_target fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so prediction metadata travels with the fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"New tiny combinational predictor for direct control flow: JAL taken, backward conditional branches taken, forward branches and JALR not taken, with target alignment gating.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the predictor to select the next fetch PC when the instruction bus is ready and carry the prediction bits in the IF output.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch prediction metadata into ID/EX alongside the decoded instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare actual resolved next PC against the predicted next PC and assert redirect only for mispredictions or unpredicted JALR/direct misses.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Preserve the existing redirect recovery behavior while treating the new redirect signal as a misprediction flush instead of every taken branch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the predictor-aware fetch and execute interfaces through the top-level pipeline.\"\n  - file: test/test_branch_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for backward taken prediction, loop-exit recovery, JAL prediction, JALR recovery, and misaligned-target trap behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
