{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r2s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r2s2\ntitle: \"Tiny PC-indexed BTB predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The previous predictor attempt showed that decoding imem_data in fetch and\n  adding a branch immediate target directly into the PC update path can destroy\n  Fmax. However, CoreMark still has enough loop branches and direct control\n  transfers that avoiding EX redirect bubbles is attractive if the prediction\n  path is kept short. A predictor indexed only by the current PC should preserve\n  most of the champion's timing while recovering cycles on repeated taken\n  branches and jumps.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small direct-mapped BTB/BHT updated in EX and consulted in IF by\n  PC bits only. Each entry stores a valid bit, a short tag, a predicted target,\n  and a 2-bit taken counter or unconditional bit. Fetch chooses either pc+4 or\n  the stored target on a tag hit without looking at imem_data, so the failed\n  imem_data-to-immediate-to-PC combinational path from the prior predictor is\n  avoided. Carry the predicted next PC through IF/ID and ID/EX; EX computes the\n  architectural next PC for branches and jumps, updates the predictor, and only\n  redirects/flushes when predicted_next_pc differs from the resolved next PC.\n  This should improve iterations per cycle on hot CoreMark loops with a modest\n  predictor table cost and much lower Fmax risk than decode-time prediction.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add predicted next-PC metadata to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so EX can compare prediction against resolved control flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/btb_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny PC-indexed direct-mapped BTB/BHT with valid/tag/target/counter state, IF lookup, and EX update ports.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use only current PC plus BTB lookup state to choose the next fetch PC, and emit the chosen predicted next PC with the fetched instruction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted next PC into ID/EX alongside decoded control signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve actual next PC, update the predictor for branch and jump instructions, and redirect only on prediction mismatch.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep existing flush and stall priorities while treating redirects as prediction-recovery events.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the predictor lookup/update and predicted-next-PC metadata through the existing single-issue pipeline.\"\n  - file: test/test_btb_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused tests for BTB hit/miss behavior, counter updates, loop-exit recovery, JAL/JALR target learning, and reset state.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
