t/instruction, and a 2-bit counter updated by resolved conditional branches.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use only the current PC and loop predictor hit state to choose the next fetch PC, avoiding any imem_data decode or immediate add in IF.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the prediction metadata through decode alongside the instruction so EX can compare prediction against the resolved branch result.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Resolve actual next PC, suppress redirect on verified correct loop predictions, recover on loop exits or aliases, and emit predictor update information.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep the existing stall and flush priorities while interpreting redirect as prediction recovery rather than every taken loop branch.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup, metadata, and EX update signals through the single-issue core without changing the top-level IO or nret=1 RVFI contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_loop_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage for trained loop prediction, loop-exit recovery, alias recovery, reset state, and unchanged behavior for forward branches and jumps.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
