{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r4s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r4s2\ntitle: \"Ahead-latched next-PC predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark has enough taken loop and\n  direct-control traffic to save several percent of cycles, but every design\n  that put a predictor lookup, immediate decode, tag compare, or target mux\n  directly on the IF PC-update path lost too much Fmax. The single-entry\n  loop predictor was close to break-even, suggesting the remaining opportunity\n  is to preserve its redirect-bubble savings while removing its lookup cone\n  from the cycle that updates the PC.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny trained next-PC predictor whose lookup result is registered one\n  fetch ahead. While fetching instruction PC, the frontend computes and latches\n  the predicted next PC for the next sequential fetch address; when that next\n  instruction is fetched, the PC register advances through a short mux fed by\n  the already-registered predicted next PC rather than by a live tag/table/\n  counter/target path. Use two very small direct-mapped entries trained by EX\n  on taken backward conditional branches and direct JAL targets, and carry only\n  predicted_next_pc plus a valid/taken bit with the instruction. EX already\n  computes the resolved next PC, so it can redirect only when the latched\n  prediction differs and can update the entries on real control-flow outcomes.\n  This targets the cycle reduction seen in the BTB and loop-predictor trials\n  while keeping the IF PC path close to the current pc+4-or-redirect mux.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add compact predicted-next-PC metadata fields to IF/ID and ID/EX so EX can verify a latched prediction against the resolved next PC.\"\n  - file: rtl/ahead_npc_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny two-entry predictor with registered look-ahead output, EX update for taken backward branches and JAL targets, and conservative reset/default-to-pc+4 behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Replace live predictor lookup in the PC update path with an already-latched predicted next PC, while precomputing the next cycle's prediction off the critical PC-select path.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch predicted-next-PC metadata alongside the decoded instruction without changing invalid-fetch bubble handling.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare resolved next PC with the carried predicted next PC, suppress redirects on correct predictions, recover on mismatches, and emit predictor update information.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep existing stall and flush priorities while treating redirect as prediction recovery rather than every taken branch or JAL.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor look-ahead, metadata, and EX update signals through the single-issue core without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_ahead_npc_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for trained loop prediction, direct JAL prediction, loop-exit recovery, alias recovery, stalls, and reset default behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
