{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261003-003-r5s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261003-003-r5s2\ntitle: \"Outstanding loop target predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark can save about four to six\n  percent of cycles when hot taken control-flow bubbles are avoided, but they\n  lost because target lookup and especially predicted-next-PC metadata widened\n  the timing-sensitive fetch/execute path. The closest attempt was the\n  single-entry loop predictor; its remaining weakness was carrying predicted\n  instruction and 32-bit target fields through the pipeline just to verify a\n  prediction two stages later.\nhypothesis: |\n  Rebuild the single-entry backward-branch target predictor around one global\n  outstanding-prediction record instead of per-instruction prediction payloads.\n  IF uses a one-entry full-PC tag, aligned target, and 2-bit counter trained by\n  EX on taken backward conditional branches; on a hit it redirects fetch to the\n  stored target and records {valid, predicted_pc, predicted_target} in a small\n  scoreboard while disabling further predictions until that branch resolves.\n  EX recomputes the architectural next PC as it already does, treats a matching\n  outstanding record as a correctly predicted redirect, and only flushes on a\n  mismatch or on ordinary unpredicted taken control flow. Because the predicted\n  target is held in one side register rather than in IF/ID and ID/EX bundles,\n  this should keep the cycle savings of the near-break-even loop predictor\n  while removing the wide verification metadata that hurt Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/loop_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry backward-branch target predictor with a 2-bit counter plus a single outstanding prediction scoreboard register.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consult the one-entry predictor by current PC, select the stored target on a confident hit, and avoid changing IF/ID payload fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compare the resolved next PC against the outstanding prediction record, suppress redirects on matches, recover on mismatches, and emit train/clear events.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep existing stall and flush priorities while treating redirect as prediction recovery or unpredicted taken control flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup, outstanding-record control, and EX training signals without changing the top-level nret=1 IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_loop_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover trained loop prediction, loop-exit recovery, stale-instruction recovery through resolved-next-PC mismatch, stalls, and reset behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
