{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r10s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r10s0\ntitle: \"Split rare writeback result lane\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's remaining worst path still runs from the register-file\n  operand path through EX's ordinary ALU and into the EX/MEM alu_result\n  register. Recent wins already removed divider, high-multiply, low-multiply,\n  and load/store address work from the common ALU cone, but ex_stage still\n  feeds alu_result through a priority mux that also handles JAL/JALR link\n  values and all completed M-sidecar results. CoreMark's steady-state integer\n  operations should not pay that mux depth on every ALU writeback.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a separate rare-result lane beside ex_mem_t.alu_result for values that do\n  not come from the ordinary one-cycle ALU: JAL/JALR pc+4, low MUL, high MUL,\n  and DIV/REM sidecar completions. Register alu_result directly from the ALU for\n  common RV32I arithmetic/logical/shift/LUI/AUIPC results, while registering the\n  sidecar/link value into a new side_result field with a compact side_result_valid\n  predicate. Select between the registered ALU result, registered side result,\n  and load data later in the forwarding/writeback path, where the source values\n  are already flopped. This should shorten the RF -> EX ALU -> EX/MEM setup path\n  without changing branch policy, memory handshakes, RVFI ordering, or CoreMark\n  instruction count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add side_result and side_result_valid fields to EX/MEM and MEM/WB bundles so rare non-ALU writeback values travel outside the hot alu_result register input.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Drive reg_q.alu_result directly from the one-cycle ALU and place JAL/JALR link values plus MUL/DIV/MULH sidecar completions into the new side-result lane.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Use a registered EX/MEM bypass-data mux that chooses side_result only for rare side-lane writers while keeping ordinary ALU forwarding intact.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Propagate the side-result lane through MEM/WB alongside existing load data and RVFI fields without changing dmem behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Extend the writeback mux to prefer load data for loads, side_result for side-lane writers, and alu_result for ordinary ALU results.\"\n  - file: test/test_side_result_forwarding.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for immediate consumers of JAL link values and M-sidecar results to protect the revised forwarding/writeback selection.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
