{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r12s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r12s0\ntitle: \"Sidecar shifter off ALU path\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's timed path is still the RF/ID operand path through\n  the execute ALU into the EX/MEM alu_result register. Prior successful\n  changes improved Fmax by removing bulky but not-every-cycle arithmetic from\n  that cone, while attempts that reshaped the ALU control or forwarding muxes\n  regressed. The remaining RV32I barrel shifter is a plausible source of the\n  15-cell ALU path, and it is separable without touching fetch prediction,\n  memory handshakes, or the single-retire RVFI contract.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move SLL, SRL, and SRA, including their immediate forms, out of rtl/alu.sv\n  into a small registered shift sidecar controlled by EX. The normal ALU keeps\n  ADD/SUB, logic, set-less-than, LUI, and the existing ALTOPS-only M formulas,\n  while EX starts the shifter for legal shift operations, injects bubbles while\n  the one-cycle result is captured, and then writes that result into EX/MEM.\n  This should remove the wide variable-shift network from the ordinary\n  ALU-result setup path; CoreMark will pay an extra cycle only on actual shift\n  instructions, so a moderate Fmax gain can beat the IPC loss if shifts are not\n  dominant.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove real SLL/SRL/SRA datapaths from the hot combinational ALU while preserving other RV32I operations and ALTOPS M substitutes.\"\n  - file: rtl/shift_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a small registered RV32I shifter sidecar with start/done/accept handshaking for left, logical-right, and arithmetic-right shifts.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Detect legal shift operations, start the shifter, hold EX until its result is ready, and select the completed shift result for EX/MEM writeback.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Reuse the existing EX busy stall path for shift sidecar waits so younger instructions and fetch state are held consistently.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the shift busy behavior through the existing EX busy interface without changing the top-level IO or nret=1 RVFI ports.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Update or extend focused ALU/execute tests so all shift variants still produce RV32I-correct results after leaving the combinational ALU.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
