ion; keep one outstanding\\nregistered predicted target for EX to verify, so stale entries and loop exits\\nrecover through the existing redirect/flush path. This should avoid the failed\\nimem_data-to-PC and full predicted_next_pc paths while retaining most of the\\ncycle reduction from the near-break-even direct branch predictor.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl\n…[12733 of 15805 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f48c16546cbdedf2]…\nes/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:229:    jalr_sum    = rs1 + in.imm;\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:230:    jump_target = in.ctrl.is_jalr ? {jalr_sum[31:1], 1'b0}\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:231:                                  : (in.pc + in.imm);\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:245:    misalign_branch = in.ctrl.is_branch && branch_taken\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:247:    misalign_jump   = in.ctrl.is_jump && (jump_target[1:0] != 2'b00);\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:258:  assign redirect_target = in.ctrl.is_jump ? jump_target : branch_target;\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:280:      reg_q.alu_result    <= in.ctrl.is_jump ? (in.pc + 32'd4)\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:303:      // pc_next reverts to pc+4 on misalign trap so the pc_fwd checker\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:306:      reg_q.pc_next       <= misalign_fault     ? (in.pc + 32'd4)\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:307:                            : in.ctrl.is_jump   ? jump_target\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv:309:                                                : (in.pc + 32'd4);\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
