ovide compact uses_rs1 and\nuses_rs2 predicates, and hazard_unit should compare a load destination only\nagainst architecturally live source operands while also ignoring invalid\nIF/ID work. This removes the EX redirect -> IF instruction mux -> decode /\nhazard dependency from the ID/EX control path and avoids false stalls on\nimmediate instructions whose imm[4:0] happens to match a preceding load rd.\nThe existing one-cycle true load-use interlock, dmem hold behavior, DIV/REM\nbusy stall, and nret=1 RVFI contract remain unchanged.\n\nLESSON: - \n…[4055 of 7127 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7be6f727a7aa7c45]…\nrs1/rs2 pair that fans out to\nthe ALU, branch comparator, JALR target adder, load/store address lane,\nstore-data path, RVFI source capture, and M sidecars. The ordinary ALU lane\nshould receive dedicated rs1_alu/rs2_alu wires used only for alu_a/alu_b and\nthe EX/MEM alu_result setup path; branch/jump, effective-address, store-data,\nand sidecar/RVFI lanes get their own duplicate muxes using the unchanged\nfwd_rs*_sel encoding. This should reduce data-net fanout and placement\npressure on the hot RF-to-ALU path without adding new bypass sources, stalls,\npredictor metadata, or result-priority muxing, so CoreMark cycles should stay\nunchanged while Fmax has a chance to clear the replacement threshold.\n\nLESSON: - 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-002-r13s1 (regression, +0.00%): Replicating EX forwarded-operand muxes into ALU, branch, memory, store-data, RVFI, and M-sidecar lanes did not improve CoreMark, implying the shared `rs1`/`rs2` fanout is not the binding RF-to-ALU cost once the load/store address lane is already split.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
