{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r6s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Source-aware EX operand mux slimming\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current best core is still limited by a short ID/EX-to-EX ALU timing path,\n  after cold DIV/REM and high-half multiply logic were successfully moved out of\n  the hot lane. Prior micro-opts that added a parallel ADD path, explicit shared\n  carry control, or a separate MUL result path regressed because they introduced\n  more result-priority muxing. A safer remaining target is the operand side of EX:\n  every instruction currently pays for forwarding muxes and an AUIPC pc-vs-rs1\n  mux even when the decoded instruction does not architecturally consume that\n  register source.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make the EX operand muxing source-aware without adding a new result datapath.\n  Gate forwarding selections with the already-decoded uses_rs1/uses_rs2 bits so\n  unused immediate fields cannot trigger false EX/MEM or MEM/WB operand selects.\n  For AUIPC, preload the ID/EX rs1_val execution copy with the instruction PC and\n  rely on the uses_rs1-gated forward unit to leave it untouched; then remove the\n  32-bit is_auipc ? pc : rs1 mux from the EX ALU A input. Keep RVFI source\n  reporting unchanged by preserving uses_rs1 as false for AUIPC and using the\n  existing RVFI-only regfile read fallback. This should shorten the common ALU,\n  load/store address, and branch-compare input cone while preserving single-cycle\n  latency and avoiding the result-mux penalties seen in earlier attempts.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 inputs and force no-forward selects when the corresponding decoded source operand is not architecturally live.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch AUIPC's execution rs1_val as the current PC while keeping uses_rs1 false for RVFI/source semantics; optionally zero unused execution source addresses only if formal remains clean.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove the AUIPC-specific ALU A mux and consume the source-aware forwarded rs1 value directly, leaving branch target and jump target PC arithmetic unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the ID/EX uses_rs1 and uses_rs2 predicates into the revised forward unit without changing the top-level nret=1 IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_hazard.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage that AUIPC ignores forwarding aliases and that ordinary rs1/rs2 forwarding, stores, branches, and load-use interlocks still behave correctly.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
