{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-001-r7s0.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"ID-normalized ALU operands\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion is limited by the short regfile/ID-to-EX/ALU path after\n  cold divider and high-half multiply work has already been removed from the\n  common lane. Recent micro-optimizations that added result muxing, predictor\n  metadata, or uses-gated forwarding lost timing, so the remaining opportunity\n  should remove EX-stage muxing without adding new bypass priority logic.\nhypothesis: |\n  Normalize the execution operands for LUI, AUIPC, and other source-less\n  instructions in ID, while preserving raw instruction source fields for RVFI.\n  Carry separate compact execution source addresses/values in ID/EX: force\n  source-less operands to x0, preload AUIPC's execution rs1 value with pc, and\n  preload LUI's execution rs1 value with zero. With those operands already\n  canonicalized, EX can use the forwarded rs1 value directly instead of a\n  32-bit is_auipc ? pc : rs1 mux, and ALU_LUI can be removed or folded into\n  ADD with rs1=0 and b=imm. Because the forward unit still compares ordinary\n  five-bit execution source addresses rather than extra uses_rs gates, this\n  keeps the hot forwarding control as shallow as the current champion while\n  trimming one ALU input mux and one ALU result-select arm from the common\n  CoreMark address/add/branch path.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Split ID/EX bookkeeping as needed so EX has normalized execution source addresses/values while RVFI can still report the raw architectural source fields.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Canonicalize execution operands during decode: AUIPC uses pc as rs1, LUI and source-less instructions use x0/zero, and RVFI source metadata remains unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Remove the AUIPC-specific ALU-A mux and feed the forwarded normalized rs1 value directly into the ALU.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Fold LUI into the existing ADD/pass-immediate behavior or remove the dedicated ALU_LUI result arm after ID supplies rs1=zero and imm as operand B.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Keep the existing simple EX/MEM and MEM/WB priority comparisons, consuming normalized execution source addresses instead of adding uses_rs gating.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire any renamed execution-source bundle fields through the unchanged nret=1 top-level core interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_hazard.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage that AUIPC and LUI ignore false forwarding aliases while ordinary ALU, load/store, branch, and load-use forwarding behavior stays intact.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
