{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r11s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r11s1\ntitle: \"Operand-isolated execute lanes\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion's worst path still runs through ID/regfile output, EX\n  forwarding and the compact ALU before landing in EX/MEM. Prior attempts show\n  that adding predictors, broad extra bypasses, or a generic EX1/EX2 split tends\n  to reintroduce more control or forwarding depth than it saves. The promising\n  structural direction is to narrow the ordinary execute cone itself without\n  changing branch recovery or making CoreMark's common low-half MUL slower.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the EX stage into small operation-family lanes selected before the\n  32-bit arithmetic result mux: an add/sub/equality lane, a logic/shift lane,\n  a compare lane, and the existing side lanes for load/store effective address\n  and cold M operations. Decode should carry a compact lane select in the\n  pipeline bundle so the ALU no longer has one wide case tree that mixes every\n  RV32I operation, branch comparison, low MUL placeholder, and LUI path into the\n  same result cone. Branches can use the add/sub/equality and compare lane\n  outputs directly, while writeback selects only among the small lane results\n  at the EX/MEM boundary. This is expected to reduce the ID-to-EX/MEM timing\n  depth more safely than full retiming because it preserves the single-cycle\n  producer/consumer forwarding contract and avoids new frontend PC logic.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a compact execute-lane select field to ctrl_t for arithmetic, logic/shift, compare, LUI/AUIPC/JAL, and M-sidecar result families.\"\n  - file: rtl/decoder.sv\n    description: \"Drive the new lane select alongside the existing alu_op while keeping illegal-instruction defaults and all opcode validation unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Refactor the monolithic ALU into smaller lane outputs or a lane-selected result path that keeps common ADD/SUB/logic/shift/compare cones independent.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the lane select to choose branch conditions and EX/MEM alu_result from the narrow lane outputs, preserving existing forwarding, M-sidecar stalls, and effective-address side lane.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Extend ALU/unit coverage for the lane-selected results so every RV32I operation and ALTOPS M substitute still matches the architectural result.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
