{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r12s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Cold shift compare sidecar\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current champion has already peeled DIV/REM, high multiply, low MUL,\n  and load/store address generation out of the ordinary execute result path.\n  The remaining worst path still lands in EX/MEM alu_result through the compact\n  RV32I ALU, where every ADD/logical operation still pays timing for the barrel\n  shifter and SLT/SLTU carry/compare result selection. Prior ALU recoding and\n  one-hot lane attempts did not help because they kept all result families in\n  the same single-cycle writeback mux.\nhypothesis: |\n  Move the cold RV32I shift and set-less-than result families out of the\n  ordinary one-cycle ALU result lane into a short registered EX sidecar. Keep\n  ADD/SUB, AND/OR/XOR, LUI, AUIPC, branch comparison, jump target generation,\n  load/store effective-address generation, and the existing M sidecars\n  unchanged. For SLL/SRL/SRA/SLT/SLTU and their immediate forms, EX starts the\n  sidecar, holds the instruction with the existing ex_busy mechanism for one\n  extra cycle, then writes the registered sidecar result into EX/MEM. This\n  should remove the wide barrel-shifter and compare-select load from the common\n  alu_result setup path while adding stalls only to less frequent operations,\n  avoiding frontend predictors, extra bypass sources, or a full pipeline\n  retime.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Restrict the hot combinational ALU to ADD/SUB, logic, LUI/AUIPC-style results, and ALTOPS substitutes; remove real shift and SLT result selection from this lane.\"\n  - file: rtl/shift_compare_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add a small registered sidecar for SLL/SRL/SRA/SLT/SLTU with start, accept, busy, done, op, operand, and result signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Detect shift/compare ALU ops, start the new sidecar, hold EX via the existing busy protocol until its result is ready, and select that registered result into EX/MEM.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Reuse the existing ex_busy pipeline hold behavior for the shift/compare sidecar so dmem stalls and long-latency M operations preserve ordering.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the revised EX busy/result behavior without changing the top-level IO or nret=1 RVFI contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Keep focused coverage for shifted and set-less-than results through the sidecar path, including immediate forms and signed versus unsigned comparisons.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
