{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"hyp-20261004-002-r8s1|hyp-20261004-002-r9s1|hyp-20261004-001-r10s0|hyp-20261004-002-r11s1\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "24:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261004-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Registered low-MUL sidecar\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The current champion's repeated worst paths still run through the EX operand\\nmux and ALU cone. Earlier structural work showed that moving cold DIV/REM and\\nhigh-half multiply out of that cone was the only consistently useful direction,\\nwhile predictors, prefetch buffers, extra execute stages, and store buffering\\nadded more control cost than they repaid. The remaining expensive arithmetic in\\nthe hot lane is the low-half 32x32 MUL, which CoreMark uses, so it cannot simply\\nbecome a long fully blocking unit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current champion's repeated worst paths still run through the EX operand\\nmux and ALU cone. Earlier structural work showed that moving cold DIV/REM and\\nhigh-half multiply out of that cone was the only consistently useful direction,\\nwhile predictors, prefetch buffers, extra execute stages, and store buffering\\nadded more control cost than they repaid. The remaining expensive arithmetic in\\nthe hot lane is the low-half 32x32 MUL, which CoreMark uses, so it cannot simply\\nbecome a long fully blocking unit.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move low-half MUL out of the combinational ALU into a tiny registered sidecar\\nthat uses the FPGA DSP product behind a one-cycle start/done handshake, similar\\nto the existing MULH and DIV sidecars but with much shorter latency. Ordinary\\nRV32I ALU, branch, jump, and load/store address operations would no longer have\\na 32x32 multiplier on their EX/MEM setup path; a MUL instruction would hold EX\\nonly until the registered product is available, then retire through the same\\nin-order path. This is a deliberately narrower version of the failed all-MDU\\nmulticycle attempt: keep only the expensive DSP product off the hot add/compare\\npath, preserve the existing cold sidecars, and avoid adding frontend prediction\\nor new bypass loops. If Fmax improves by more than the extra MUL cycles cost,\\nCoreMark iterations/second should clear the replaceme\n…[17934 of 21006 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1561ac97b28ee5d2]…\n 134.31, \"delta_pct\": -4.0, \"vs_baseline\": 1008.17, \"fmax_mhz\": 61.584, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4585322, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2877, \"ff\": 976, \"seeds\": [59.304, 61.584, 61.584], \"perturbations\": [[0, 59.304, 15], [1, 61.584, 16], [2, 61.584, 16]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100\", \"slack_ns\": -11.862, \"arrival_ns\": 22.157, \"logic_cells\": 38, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T23:50:29.739727Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 11, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-002-r11s1 (regression, -4.00%): One-hot ALU result lanes can regress when predecode bloats the ID/EX control bundle and the final mask/OR select still fans every add/logic/shift/SLT result into EX/MEM, so a compact opcode case may synthesize to a shallower hot execute cone.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\"", "aggregated_output": "// rtl/mem_stage.sv\n//\n// Memory access stage. Drives the dmem read/write ports combinationally\n// from EX/MEM's dedicated effective-address lane, and sign/zero-extends\n// the loaded data into the MEM/WB register.\n//\n// Byte-lane discipline:\n//   - Write data is replicated across all four byte lanes; the\n//     byte-mask (mem_wmask) selects the actual destination bytes.\n//   - Load: shift the raw word right by `addr[1:0]*8`, then sign- or\n//     zero-extend the low 8/16 bits per the LB/LBU/LH/LHU encoding.\n//   - For RVFI ALIGNED_MEM, mem_addr is reported word-aligned and the\n//     byte position is captured in mem_rmask / mem_wmask.\n//\n// Latency:        1 cycle (MEM/WB register clocked here).\n// RVFI fields:    feeds mem_addr, mem_rmask, mem_wmask, mem_rdata,\n//                 mem_wdata, plus rd_wdata via the loaded-data path.\nmodule mem_stage (\n  input  logic               clock,\n  input  logic               reset,\n  // hold_wb: dmem stall is in effect. MEM/WB's data fields are RETAINED\n  // (so the previously-retired LOAD's `rd` / `read_data` / `ctrl.reg_write`\n  // remain visible to forward_unit), but `valid` is cleared so:\n  //   - rvfi_order doesn't increment for held cycles\n  //   - wb_stage doesn't write the regfile twice\n  // Zeroing the whole register would lose the LOAD's load_data, breaking\n  // MEM/WB->EX forwarding for any dependent instruction that's also held\n  // in ID/EX during the stall (e.g. a BNE that consumes a LOAD's result).\n  input  logic               hold_wb,\n  // ex_mem_t carries branch_taken / branch_target / pc_next / rs?_val\n  // for downstream RVFI use; mem_stage only consumes a subset, so the\n  // remaining fields look unused from this module's perspective.\n  /* verilator lint_off UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  input  ex_mem_t  in,\n  /* verilator lint_on UNUSEDSIGNAL */\n  // dmem interface\n  output logic [31:0]        dmem_addr,\n  output logic [31:0]        dmem_wdata,\n  input  logic [31:0]        dmem_rdata,\n  output logic [3:0]         dmem_wen,\n  output logic               dmem_ren,\n  // \n…[3210 of 6282 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7b8b54220d09abb4]…\nendent in ID/EX needs the held LOAD's rd/read_data/ctrl\n      // alive for as many cycles as the dmem stall lasts.\n      reg_q.valid <= 1'b0;\n    end else begin\n      reg_q.pc         <= in.pc;\n      reg_q.alu_result <= in.alu_result;\n      reg_q.read_data  <= load_data;\n      reg_q.rd         <= in.rd;\n      reg_q.rs1_addr   <= in.rs1_addr;\n      reg_q.rs2_addr   <= in.rs2_addr;\n      reg_q.uses_rs1   <= in.uses_rs1;\n      reg_q.uses_rs2   <= in.uses_rs2;\n      reg_q.rs1_val    <= in.rs1_val;\n      reg_q.rs2_val    <= in.rs2_val;\n      reg_q.pc_next    <= in.pc_next;\n      reg_q.mem_addr   <= aligned_addr;\n      reg_q.mem_rdata  <= dmem_rdata;\n      reg_q.mem_wdata  <= wdata_rep;\n      reg_q.mem_wmask  <= (in.ctrl.mem_write && !mem_misalign) ? byte_mask : 4'b0000;\n      reg_q.mem_rmask  <= (in.ctrl.mem_read  && !mem_misalign) ? byte_mask : 4'b0000;\n      reg_q.ctrl       <= ctrl_with_trap;\n      reg_q.instr      <= in.instr;\n      reg_q.valid      <= in.valid;\n    end\n  end\n\n  assign out = reg_q;\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
