{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-002-r15s1.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-002-r15s1\ntitle: \"Decode precomputed PC lanes\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The current accepted core is still limited by the ID/EX-to-EX/MEM execute\n  region, with recent worst paths landing in or near the compact ALU result\n  register. Prior structural attempts show that adding predictor lookup,\n  wider forwarding, or extra visible stalls tends to cost more than it saves.\n  A safer structural target is the PC-relative work still recomputed in EX for\n  jumps, branch targets, and fallthrough bookkeeping even though it depends\n  only on the fetch PC and immediate already available in decode.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add narrow precomputed PC lanes to the ID/EX bundle: pc_plus4 and direct\n  pc_plus_imm. The ID stage should compute and latch these values beside the\n  existing immediate, and EX should consume them for JAL link writeback,\n  JAL/direct-branch targets, and non-redirect fallthrough pc_next instead of\n  rebuilding those adders and mux inputs around the hot ALU/redirect logic.\n  JALR target calculation stays in EX because it depends on the forwarded rs1\n  value, and the existing load/store effective-address lane, M sidecars,\n  forwarding policy, and nret=1 top-level contract remain unchanged.\n\n  This is intended to shorten and declutter the execute structural cone without\n  changing CoreMark-visible latency. Unlike earlier predictor and EX-split\n  attempts, it does not add frontend target selection, branch metadata, or a\n  producer-consumer bypass loop. If Gowin was packing the jump link/target\n  adders and PC muxing close to the remaining ALU path, moving that work behind\n  decode flops should improve Fmax enough to clear the replacement threshold\n  while preserving the current cycle count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Extend the ID/EX payload with pc_plus4 and pc_plus_imm fields for decode-latched PC-relative values.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute pc+4 and pc+imm from the IF/ID PC and generated immediate, then latch them into ID/EX on valid instructions.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the precomputed PC lanes for JAL link results, direct branch/JAL targets, and fallthrough pc_next while keeping JALR rs1+imm resolution in EX.\"\n  - file: test/test_pc_precompute.py\n    description: \"Cover JAL, direct branches, branch-not-taken fallthrough, JALR forwarding, and misaligned-target trap behavior with the precomputed PC lanes.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
