{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"store buffer|write buffer|nonblocking store|store queue|dmem stall|dmem_ready|memory op|buffer\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl cores/bench/LESSONS.md'", "aggregated_output": "cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl:6:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-002-r2s1\", \"title\": \"Registered IF/ID control boundary\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"After the iterative divider improvement, the timed critical path is no\\nlonger dominated by RV32M arithmetic. The reported worst path now loops\\nthrough decode, execute redirect generation, fetch flush selection, the\\nhazard unit, and back into the ID/EX register enable/data mux. The current\\nIF/ID payload is combinational, so branch redirect, imem stall, load-use\\ndetection, and ID/EX capture all sit in one broad control cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"After the iterative divider improvement, the timed critical path is no\\nlonger dominated by RV32M arithmetic. The reported worst path now loops\\nthrough decode, execute redirect generation, fetch flush selection, the\\nhazard unit, and back into the ID/EX register enable/data mux. The current\\nIF/ID payload is combinational, so branch redirect, imem stall, load-use\\ndetection, and ID/EX capture all sit in one broad control cone.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a real IF/ID pipeline register and restructure stall/flush handling so\\ndecode consumes a stable registered instruction instead of the same-cycle\\nimem_data/redirect mux output. The PC should still update immediately on an\\nEX redirect, but wrong-path instructions are killed by clearing the IF/ID\\nvalid bit and ID/EX valid bit at their stage boundaries. Hazard detection\\nshould use the registered IF/ID rs fields, with IF/ID held on downstream\\nstalls and loaded with a bubble when imem is not ready. This breaks the\\ncurrent combinational redirect-to-fetch-to-hazard-to-ID feedback path while\\nkeeping one instruction per cycle throughput after fill and preserving the\\nexisting load-use, dmem stall, DIV/REM busy, and RVFI retirement behavior.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Keep or extend the IF/ID bundle as a true registered stage payload with pc, instr, and valid f\n…[7224 of 10296 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:586e87740079194d]…\n\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 116.31, \"delta_pct\": 0.59, \"vs_baseline\": 859.65, \"fmax_mhz\": 50.466, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4338935, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 2984, \"ff\": 922, \"seeds\": [50.286, 50.466, 50.466], \"perturbations\": [[0, 50.286, 13], [1, 50.466, 13], [2, 50.466, 13]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_2_dmem_2_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.886, \"arrival_ns\": 25.181, \"logic_cells\": 13, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 13, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T21:20:33.435962Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 3, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-03 hyp-20261003-002-r3s1 (regression, +0.59%): A fall-through IF prefetch FIFO can fail to repay its FIFO/dequeue/bypass/redirect-control cost on CoreMark when random imem bubbles and backend stalls are not long or independent enough to amortize added fetch-side control.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
