{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    o=json.loads(line)\n    if o['id'] in ['hyp-20261004-003-r6s2','hyp-20261004-003-r9s2']:\n        print('---', o['id'], o['title'])\n        h=o.get('hypothesis')\n        if isinstance(h,dict):\n            print(h.get('hypothesis'))\n            print('changes:')\n            for c in h.get('changes',[]): print(' ',c)\n        print('notes:', o.get('implementation_notes','')[:2000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "--- hyp-20261004-003-r6s2 Exact direct-branch taken predictor\nAdd a tiny exact-tag predictor for direct taken control flow, focused on\nbackward conditional branches and direct JALs. The predictor stores a full\nbranch PC tag, its deterministic target, and a small confidence bit or\ncounter; IF may use the stored target on a tag hit, but EX updates the table\nonly through registered state so training never feeds the same-cycle fetch\nlookup. Because direct branch and JAL targets are immutable for a given PC,\nthe pipeline only needs to carry a one-bit predicted_taken marker with the\ninstruction, not a 32-bit predicted target. EX suppresses the normal taken\nredirect when predicted_taken and the branch or JAL is actually taken, and\nredirects only for loop exits, unpredicted taken branches, unpredicted JALs,\nand all JALR cases. This should preserve most of the prior predictor IPC win\nwhile cutting out the wide target-compare and outstanding-record cones that\npreviously crushed Fmax.\n\nchanges:\n  {'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add a single predicted_taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so EX can suppress correctly predicted direct-taken redirects without carrying a predicted target.'}\n  {'file': 'rtl/direct_predictor.sv', 'description': 'Add a one-entry or two-entry exact-PC direct-branch predictor with registered training, full tags, stored aligned targets, and conservative reset/default-not-taken behavior.'}\n  {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Use the predictor target on a full-tag hit while keeping redirect priority and avoiding any combinational path from EX training into the same-cycle lookup.'}\n  {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Latch the one-bit predicted_taken marker with the decoded instruction and leave invalid-fetch bubble handling unchanged.'}\n  {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Suppress redirects for predicted_taken direct branches or JALs that resolve taken, redirect on predicted loop exits or unpredicted taken control flow, and emit registered predictor training\n…[1818 of 4890 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:dfa7b06fe44e925a]…\nered EX training.'}\n  {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Consult the direct predictor by current PC, select its target only on a confident exact hit, and keep EX redirect priority over prediction.'}\n  {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Latch the predicted_taken marker through decode while preserving invalid-fetch bubble handling and existing stall semantics.'}\n  {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Train only backward taken conditional branches and direct JALs, suppress redirects on correct predicted-taken direct control flow, and recover on loop exits or stale predictions.'}\n  {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire predictor lookup, one-bit metadata, and registered training through the single-issue core without changing the nret=1 top-level IO.'}\n  {'file': 'test/test_direct_predictor.py', 'description': 'Cover trained backward-loop hits, loop-exit recovery, direct JAL hits, stale-entry recovery, reset default-not-taken behavior, and stalls around predicted branches.'}\nnotes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
