{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r11s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r11s2\ntitle: \"Retire-trained sequential predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior branch predictors recovered some CoreMark cycles but repeatedly lost\n  Fmax by adding combinational lookup, target selection, EX training, or target\n  verification to the already fragile fetch/redirect path. The near-break-even\n  direct predictors suggest the IPC opportunity is real, but the predictor must\n  be decoupled from EX and from same-cycle instruction decode to have a chance\n  of clearing the champion by more than placement noise.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny direct-control predictor whose table is trained only from retired\n  MEM/WB state and whose fetch decision uses only a prediction registered during\n  the previous sequential fetch cycle. Lookup for the next sequential PC\n  produces a registered hit/target for the following cycle; redirects and\n  predicted-taken jumps simply invalidate that registered prediction for one\n  cycle rather than feeding redirect targets into the predictor. Train only\n  taken backward conditional branches and direct JALs, and carry a single\n  predicted_taken bit to EX so correctly predicted direct-taken control flow\n  suppresses the normal redirect while loop exits redirect back to pc+4. This\n  should keep the IF PC mux to a registered target select and remove the EX to\n  predictor path that sank the ahead-registered design, while still eliminating\n  repeat loop/JAL redirect bubbles in CoreMark.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit predicted_taken field to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles; do not carry predicted targets or instruction copies through the pipe.\"\n  - file: rtl/retire_direct_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry or two-entry exact direct-control predictor with registered sequential lookup, retired MEM/WB training, aligned targets, and conservative confidence.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select a registered prediction target only when the previous sequential lookup hit, invalidate prediction on redirects or predicted-taken transfers, and keep redirect priority unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted_taken bit through decode while preserving invalid-fetch bubble and stall behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress redirects only for predicted direct control flow that actually resolves taken; redirect to pc+4 on predicted loop exits or stale non-taken cases.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup state and retired training from MEM/WB without adding EX combinational training or redirect-target lookup paths.\"\n  - file: test/test_retire_direct_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover retired-only training, sequential registered lookup timing, loop hits, loop exits, direct JAL hits, redirect invalidation, and imem/dmem stall interactions.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
