{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r12s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r12s2\ntitle: \"JAL-only static fast predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark has a real control-flow IPC\n  opportunity, but table lookups, target metadata, EX target verification,\n  and return-stack logic have repeatedly cost more Fmax than they saved. The\n  remaining predictor angle worth trying is the smallest direct-control case:\n  unconditional JAL and compiler-emitted J pseudo-branches have a target that\n  is exact from the fetched instruction, never need a direction decision, and\n  can suppress the later EX redirect without carrying a 32-bit predicted PC.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a static JAL-only predictor in fetch that recognizes opcode 1101111,\n  computes the J immediate target, and uses it as the next PC only when the\n  instruction fetch is valid and the target is word-aligned. Carry a single\n  predicted_jal bit with the instruction into EX. In EX, suppress the normal\n  redirect for a valid, aligned, non-JALR jump only when that bit is set; all\n  conditional branches, JALR returns, loop exits, stale fetches, and misaligned\n  targets keep the existing EX redirect or trap behavior. This avoids BTB/BHT\n  state, tags, confidence counters, RAS update paths, and predicted-target\n  comparisons while eliminating the two-bubble redirect penalty for repeated\n  direct calls and unconditional JAL branches in CoreMark. The expected gain is\n  modest but the Fmax risk is much lower than prior learned predictors because\n  the only new hot fetch logic is a narrow opcode check, J-immediate adder, and\n  a one-bit pipeline tag.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit predicted_jal field to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles; do not carry a predicted target.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize valid aligned JAL instructions, choose the computed target as next PC, and emit predicted_jal with redirect priority preserved.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted_jal bit through decode while preserving existing stall, flush, invalid-fetch, and illegal-instruction behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress the normal jump redirect only for aligned non-JALR jumps tagged predicted_jal; keep misaligned traps and JALR redirects unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the widened pipeline bundles without changing the top-level nret=1 IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_jal_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover JAL prediction hits, J pseudo-branches, misaligned-target trap gating, JALR non-prediction, redirects during stalls, and RVFI pc_wdata consistency.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
