{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r14s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r14s2\ntitle: \"ID link-register JALR predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts repeatedly lost Fmax by putting table lookup,\n  immediate decode, target muxing, or predicted-target verification on the\n  fetch and EX redirect paths. CoreMark still pays the full EX redirect\n  penalty on every JALR return, even though return targets usually come from\n  stable link registers whose values are already known before execute.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a narrow ID-stage predictor for JALR instructions whose base register is\n  x1 or x5. Maintain exact shadow values for those link registers from the\n  writeback stream, bypassing same-cycle writeback and refusing to predict\n  when ID/EX or EX/MEM has an unresolved writer to the selected link register.\n  When decode sees a valid, un-stalled, aligned JALR using a clean link value,\n  it redirects fetch one cycle earlier to `(link_value + imm) & ~1` and carries\n  only a one-bit `predicted_jalr` tag into EX. EX suppresses the normal JALR\n  redirect only for a tagged, non-trapping JALR; misaligned targets, dirty link\n  dependencies, non-link-register JALR, and all conditional branches keep the\n  current EX redirect and trap behavior. This targets the frequent return path\n  without BTB/BHT/RAS state, without a fetch-time instruction predictor, and\n  without carrying or comparing a 32-bit predicted target through the pipeline.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit predicted_jalr field to the ID/EX payload; do not add predicted target metadata.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Maintain exact x1/x5 link-register shadow values with writeback bypass, detect unresolved link-register writers, and wire an ID early-redirect path into fetch.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Accept an ID-stage early redirect target with lower priority than EX redirect and higher priority than sequential PC update, preserving existing stall and flush semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Recognize clean link-register JALR instructions, compute aligned early targets from the shadow value plus immediate, emit the early redirect, and latch predicted_jalr into ID/EX.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress the normal JALR redirect only for tagged predicted_jalr instructions that do not trap; leave misalignment and non-predicted recovery unchanged.\"\n  - file: test/test_link_jalr_predictor.py\n    description: \"Cover predicted returns, dirty link-register dependency blocking, same-cycle writeback bypass, misaligned target trap preservation, and RVFI pc_wdata continuity.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
