{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'rg -n \"predictor|predict|BTB|BHT|RAS|JALR|loop|return|branch\" cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Iterative divider off ALU critical path\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows the worst path entering the EX forwarding\\nmuxes and then the monolithic ALU. The current ALU keeps RV32M DIV/REM in\\nthe same combinational result mux as ADD, branch compare support, and memory\\naddress generation, so every common integer operation pays timing for a rare\\nslow operation. CoreMark's hot path is dominated by simple ALU, load/store,\\nand branch work, making the divider a high-value target for a focused\\ntiming micro-optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline timing report shows the worst path entering the EX forwarding\\nmuxes and then the monolithic ALU. The current ALU keeps RV32M DIV/REM in\\nthe same combinational result mux as ADD, branch compare support, and memory\\naddress generation, so every common integer operation pays timing for a rare\\nslow operation. CoreMark's hot path is dominated by simple ALU, load/store,\\nand branch work, making the divider a high-value target for a focused\\ntiming micro-optimization.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU out of the combinational ALU and into a small\\niterative divide/remainder unit controlled by EX. Keep ADD/SUB/logic/shift,\\ncompare, multiply, load/store address, and jump return generation on the\\nexisting single-cycle path, but assert an EX-local stall only while a divide\\nor remainder instruction is in flight. Under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS, preserve\\nthe existing combinational substitute formulas so the fast formal checks keep\\ntheir current behavior. Removing the divider cone from the normal ALU mux\\nshould substantially improve Fmax while adding cycles only for rare RV32M\\ndivision instructions.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 25, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real DIV/REM arithmetic from the normal combinational ALU path while retaining RV32I operations, MUL variants, and ALTOPS substitutes.\"}, {\n…[204964 of 208036 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:675ca1ae71de303b]…\n42.46, \"delta_pct\": 1.82, \"vs_baseline\": 1075.41, \"fmax_mhz\": 65.144, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4572835, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3195, \"ff\": 1056, \"seeds\": [61.436, 65.144, 65.144], \"perturbations\": [[0, 61.436, 15], [1, 65.144, 15], [2, 65.144, 15]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_1_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -11.277, \"arrival_ns\": 21.571, \"logic_cells\": 15, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 15, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T00:41:15.478290Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 14, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-003-r14s2 (regression, +1.82%): Even an exact link-register-only JALR predictor can regress if the ID `link_x*_dirty`/WB-bypass checks, `link_value+imm` target adder, `rs1_val` override, and added IF PC-select path cost more than CoreMark's saved return redirect bubbles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
