{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, textwrap\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    e=json.loads(line)\n    if e.get('id')=='hyp-20261004-003-r12s2':\n        for k in ['id','title','outcome','delta_pct','fmax_mhz','cycles','lut4','ff','critical_path','implementation_notes','lesson']:\n            print(k, ':', e.get(k))\n        h=e.get('hypothesis')\n        if isinstance(h, dict):\n            print('\\\\nHYPOTHESIS:\\\\n', h.get('hypothesis'))\n            print('\\\\nCHANGES:')\n            for c in h.get('changes',[]): print(c)\n        else:\n            print('\\\\nHYPOTHESIS:\\\\n', h)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"id : hyp-20261004-003-r12s2\ntitle : JAL-only static fast predictor\noutcome : regression\ndelta_pct : -6.36\nfmax_mhz : 59.443\ncycles : 4537175\nlut4 : 3133\nff : 962\ncritical_path : {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_0_s100', 'slack_ns': -12.296, 'arrival_ns': 22.59, 'logic_cells': 38, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id']}\nimplementation_notes : \nlesson : None\n\nHYPOTHESIS:\n Add a static JAL-only predictor in fetch that recognizes opcode 1101111,\ncomputes the J immediate target, and uses it as the next PC only when the\ninstruction fetch is valid and the target is word-aligned. Carry a single\npredicted_jal bit with the instruction into EX. In EX, suppress the normal\nredirect for a valid, aligned, non-JALR jump only when that bit is set; all\nconditional branches, JALR returns, loop exits, stale fetches, and misaligned\ntargets keep the existing EX redirect or trap behavior. This avoids BTB/BHT\nstate, tags, confidence counters, RAS update paths, and predicted-target\ncomparisons while eliminating the two-bubble redirect penalty for repeated\ndirect calls and unconditional JAL branches in CoreMark. The expected gain is\nmodest but the Fmax risk is much lower than prior learned predictors because\nthe only new hot fetch logic is a narrow opcode check, J-immediate adder, and\na one-bit pipeline tag.\n\n\nCHANGES:\n{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add a one-bit predicted_jal field to IF/ID and ID/EX bundles; do not carry a predicted target.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Recognize valid aligned JAL instructions, choose the computed target as next PC, and emit predicted_jal with redirect priority preserved.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Latch the predicted_jal bit through decode while preserving existing stall, flush, invalid-fetch, and illegal-instruction behavior.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Suppress the normal jump redirect only for aligned non-JALR jumps tagged predicted_jal; keep misaligned traps and JALR redirects unchanged.'}\n{'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire the widened pipeline bundles without changing the top-level nret=1 IO contract.'}\n{'file': 'test/test_jal_predictor.py', 'description': 'Cover JAL prediction hits, J pseudo-branches, misaligned-target trap gating, JALR non-prediction, redirects during stalls, and RVFI pc_wdata consistency.'}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
