{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor target in ['hyp-20261004-003-r6s2','hyp-20261004-003-r9s2','hyp-20261003-003-r3s2','hyp-20261003-003-r5s2']:\n  for line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    e=json.loads(line)\n    if e.get('id')==target:\n      h=e.get('hypothesis')\n      print('\\\\n###',target,e.get('title'),e.get('outcome'),e.get('delta_pct'))\n      print((h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)[:1400])\n      print('changes:', [c['file'] for c in (h.get('changes') if isinstance(h,dict) else e.get('changes',[]))])\n      print('critical:', e.get('critical_path'))\n      break\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_20", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor target in ['hyp-20261004-003-r6s2','hyp-20261004-003-r9s2','hyp-20261003-003-r3s2','hyp-20261003-003-r5s2']:\n  for line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    e=json.loads(line)\n    if e.get('id')==target:\n      h=e.get('hypothesis')\n      print('\\\\n###',target,e.get('title'),e.get('outcome'),e.get('delta_pct'))\n      print((h.get('hypothesis') if isinstance(h,dict) else h)[:1400])\n      print('changes:', [c['file'] for c in (h.get('changes') if isinstance(h,dict) else e.get('changes',[]))])\n      print('critical:', e.get('critical_path'))\n      break\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "\n### hyp-20261004-003-r6s2 Exact direct-branch taken predictor regression -0.12\nAdd a tiny exact-tag predictor for direct taken control flow, focused on\nbackward conditional branches and direct JALs. The predictor stores a full\nbranch PC tag, its deterministic target, and a small confidence bit or\ncounter; IF may use the stored target on a tag hit, but EX updates the table\nonly through registered state so training never feeds the same-cycle fetch\nlookup. Because direct branch and JAL targets are immutable for a given PC,\nthe pipeline only needs to carry a one-bit predicted_taken marker with the\ninstruction, not a 32-bit predicted target. EX suppresses the normal taken\nredirect when predicted_taken and the branch or JAL is actually taken, and\nredirects only for loop exits, unpredicted taken branches, unpredicted JALs,\nand all JALR cases. This should preserve most of the prior predictor IPC win\nwhile cutting out the wide target-compare and outstanding-record cones that\npreviously crushed Fmax.\n\nchanges: ['rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'rtl/direct_predictor.sv', 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'rtl/core.sv', 'test/test_direct_predictor.py']\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -14.185, 'arrival_ns': 24.48, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\n### hyp-20261004-003-r9s2 Confidence-gated loop/JAL predictor regression 0.7\nAdd a tiny exact-PC predictor trained only by resolved taken backward\nconditional branches and direct JALs. Implement it as two flop-backed entries\nwith full PC tags, aligned target PCs, and 2-bit confidence, with registered\nEX training so updates never feed the same-cycle IF lookup. IF redirects only\non an exact tag hit with strong confidence; the pipeline carries only a\none-bit predicted_taken marker, not a 32-bit predicted target. EX suppresses\nthe normal taken redirect only when that marked instruction resolves as a\ntaken direct branch or JAL, and uses the existing redire\n…[2325 of 5397 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1178dd7fbdc7fb01]…\nto the\nstored target and records {valid, predicted_pc, predicted_target} in a small\nscoreboard while disabling further predictions until that branch resolves.\nEX recomputes the architectural next PC as it already does, treats a matching\noutstanding record as a correctly predicted redirect, and only flushes on a\nmismatch or on ordinary unpredicted taken control flow. Because the predicted\ntarget is held in one side register rather than in IF/ID and ID/EX bundles,\nthis should keep the cycle savings of the near-break-even loop predictor\nwhile removing the wide verification metadata that hurt Fmax.\n\nchanges: ['rtl/loop_predictor.sv', 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'rtl/core.sv', 'test/test_loop_predictor.py']\ncritical: {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs1_val_0_s100', 'slack_ns': -17.636, 'arrival_ns': 27.93, 'logic_cells': 47, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_loop_predictor', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_id']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
