{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r6s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r6s2\ntitle: \"Exact direct-branch taken predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts found useful CoreMark cycle savings from avoiding\n  taken loop-branch bubbles, but lost badly when predictor lookup, target\n  verification, or 32-bit predicted-next-PC metadata landed on timing-critical\n  IF/EX paths. The next predictor attempt should keep the same direct-branch\n  opportunity while removing almost all verification payload and same-cycle\n  predictor feedback.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny exact-tag predictor for direct taken control flow, focused on\n  backward conditional branches and direct JALs. The predictor stores a full\n  branch PC tag, its deterministic target, and a small confidence bit or\n  counter; IF may use the stored target on a tag hit, but EX updates the table\n  only through registered state so training never feeds the same-cycle fetch\n  lookup. Because direct branch and JAL targets are immutable for a given PC,\n  the pipeline only needs to carry a one-bit predicted_taken marker with the\n  instruction, not a 32-bit predicted target. EX suppresses the normal taken\n  redirect when predicted_taken and the branch or JAL is actually taken, and\n  redirects only for loop exits, unpredicted taken branches, unpredicted JALs,\n  and all JALR cases. This should preserve most of the prior predictor IPC win\n  while cutting out the wide target-compare and outstanding-record cones that\n  previously crushed Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a single predicted_taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so EX can suppress correctly predicted direct-taken redirects without carrying a predicted target.\"\n  - file: rtl/direct_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-entry or two-entry exact-PC direct-branch predictor with registered training, full tags, stored aligned targets, and conservative reset/default-not-taken behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the predictor target on a full-tag hit while keeping redirect priority and avoiding any combinational path from EX training into the same-cycle lookup.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the one-bit predicted_taken marker with the decoded instruction and leave invalid-fetch bubble handling unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress redirects for predicted_taken direct branches or JALs that resolve taken, redirect on predicted loop exits or unpredicted taken control flow, and emit registered predictor training signals.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup, one-bit prediction metadata, and registered EX training signals through the single-issue core without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_direct_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused cocotb coverage for trained backward-branch hits, loop-exit recovery, direct JAL prediction, reset default-not-taken behavior, and stalls around predicted branches.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
