g cycles only for rare RV32M\\ndivision instructions.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 25, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove real DIV/REM arithmetic from the normal combinational ALU path while retaining RV32I operations, MUL variants, and ALTOPS substitutes.\"}, {\n…[87199 of 90271 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e981ada3e123c0b9]…\n \"delta_pct\": -0.12, \"vs_baseline\": 921.29, \"fmax_mhz\": 53.069, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4287237, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3168, \"ff\": 1093, \"seeds\": [52.123, 53.069, 53.069], \"perturbations\": [[0, 52.123, 12], [1, 53.069, 12], [2, 53.069, 12]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -14.185, \"arrival_ns\": 24.48, \"logic_cells\": 12, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T22:14:19.030084Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-003-r6s2 (regression, -0.12%): Even with one-bit `predicted_taken` metadata and registered training, an exact direct-branch/JAL predictor was only break-even because IF full-PC tag/target selection plus EX redirect gating still cost about as much as CoreMark's saved taken-control bubbles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
