{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r7s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r7s2\ntitle: \"All-direction direct branch predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  The previous exact direct-branch/JAL predictor was almost break-even: it cut\n  CoreMark cycles by predicting hot taken direct control flow, but its IF-side\n  tag/target mux cost roughly matched the IPC gain. That result suggests the\n  one-bit verification scheme is viable, but the predictor did not cover enough\n  taken branches to clear the tournament threshold. CoreMark's list, matrix,\n  and state code also contain frequently taken forward conditionals, not just\n  loop-back branches and direct JALs.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a tiny exact-tag direct branch target predictor that trains on every\n  resolved taken direct conditional branch, regardless of offset direction, as\n  well as direct JALs. Keep the r6s2-style cheap correctness contract: IF uses\n  a stored target only on a full-PC tag hit with a confident counter, and the\n  pipeline carries only a one-bit predicted_taken marker, never a 32-bit\n  predicted target. EX suppresses the normal redirect only when a direct branch\n  or JAL that was predicted taken actually resolves taken; loop exits,\n  not-taken predictions, stale entries, JALR, and illegal/misaligned cases all\n  recover through the existing redirect/flush machinery. Extending the same\n  low-metadata predictor to hot forward taken branches should improve\n  iterations/cycle enough to exceed the prior near miss while preserving most\n  of the champion's Fmax.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a single predicted_taken bit to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so EX can suppress only verified direct-taken redirects without carrying predicted targets.\"\n  - file: rtl/direct_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a small exact-PC direct target predictor with full tags, stored aligned targets, and 2-bit confidence counters trained on all taken direct branches and JALs.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select the predictor target on a confident full-tag hit while keeping EX redirect priority and avoiding any combinational path from EX training into same-cycle lookup.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the one-bit predicted_taken marker with the decoded instruction and leave invalid-fetch bubble handling unchanged.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Train the predictor from resolved direct branches/JALs, suppress redirects for predicted-taken direct control flow that resolves taken, and recover on not-taken exits or unpredicted taken cases.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Preserve existing stall and flush priorities while treating redirect as prediction recovery or unpredicted taken control flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire predictor lookup, one-bit prediction metadata, and registered EX training signals through the single-issue core without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_direct_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage for trained backward and forward branch hits, loop-exit recovery, direct JAL prediction, stale-entry recovery, stalls, and reset default-not-taken behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
