{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"predictor\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261003-003-r2s2\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261003-003-r3s2\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261003-003-r4s2\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261003-003-r5s2\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261004-003-r6s2\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261004-003-r7s2\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261003-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Static direct-control-flow predictor\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current five-stage core resolves every branch and jump in EX, then flushes\\nthe younger IF and ID work on any taken redirect. CoreMark has many loop-back\\nbranches and direct calls/jumps, so paying the full redirect penalty on every\\ntaken direct control-flow instruction leaves meaningful iterations/cycle on\\nthe table even if Fmax is unchanged. A very small predictor should improve IPC\\nwithout touching the existing critical ALU/forwarding path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The current five-stage core resolves every branch and jump in EX, then flushes\\nthe younger IF and ID work on any taken redirect. CoreMark has many loop-back\\nbranches and direct calls/jumps, so paying the full redirect penalty on every\\ntaken direct control-flow instruction leaves meaningful iterations/cycle on\\nthe table even if Fmax is unchanged. A very small predictor should improve IPC\\nwithout touching the existing critical ALU/forwarding path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a decode-time static predictor in fetch for direct control flow: predict\\nJAL as taken to its immediate target and predict conditional branches with a\\nbackward offset as taken while leaving forward branches and all JALR/returns\\npredicted not-taken. Carry predicted_taken and predicted_target with the\\ninstruction into EX, where the already-existing branch/jump resolution compares\\nactual next PC against the predicted next PC and redirects only on mismatch.\\nCorrectly predicted backward loop branches and direct JALs should retire with\\nno redirect bubbles; only loop exits, forward taken branches, JALR, and\\nmispredictions pay the current recovery cost.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 8, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add predicted_taken and predicted_target fields to the IF/ID and ID/EX bundles so prediction metadata travels with the fetched instruction.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/branch_pred\n…[39594 of 42666 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:572fad2c28de0072]…\neline\": 665.1, \"fmax_mhz\": 39.784, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4290383, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 3547, \"ff\": 983, \"seeds\": [39.681, 39.784, 39.784], \"perturbations\": [[0, 39.681, 25], [1, 39.784, 25], [2, 39.784, 25]], \"lutram\": 51, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 2, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s95\", \"slack_ns\": -20.201, \"arrival_ns\": 30.495, \"logic_cells\": 66, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_if\", \"cpu/u_id\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 25, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-03T22:37:59.709312Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 7, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-10-04 hyp-20261004-003-r7s2 (regression, -25.18%): Extending the exact direct-control predictor to all taken branch directions can turn CoreMark's forward conditionals into costly wrong-path fetches, so IF full-PC tag/target muxing plus EX `predicted_taken` recovery needs stronger bias filtering than a tiny direct table provides.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
