{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261004-003-r8s2.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261004-003-r8s2\ntitle: \"Tiny return-address predictor\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Prior predictor attempts show that CoreMark has exploitable taken-control\n  bubbles, but fetch-stage branch target tables and forward-conditional\n  prediction can cost as much Fmax as they save in cycles. The closest result\n  was the exact direct branch/JAL predictor, which was almost break-even while\n  still leaving every JALR return to pay the current EX redirect penalty. A\n  return-focused predictor targets a different high-frequency control-flow\n  class without predicting hard-to-filter forward conditionals.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a very small return-address predictor: a 2-entry or 4-entry RAS updated\n  by resolved call/return instructions plus a tiny learned return-PC filter so\n  IF only redirects from PCs that have previously retired as return-style JALR\n  instructions. On a return-PC tag hit, fetch uses the RAS top as the next PC\n  and carries only a predicted_return bit with the instruction; a single\n  outstanding return record holds the predicted target until EX recomputes the\n  JALR target and either suppresses the redirect on a match or recovers through\n  the existing flush path on a mismatch. This should recover repeated function\n  return bubbles in CoreMark while avoiding the all-direction branch predictor's\n  forward-conditional wrong-path traffic and avoiding wide per-instruction\n  predicted-next-PC metadata.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Add a one-bit predicted_return field to IF/ID and ID/EX so return predictions can be verified without carrying a predicted target through the pipeline.\"\n  - file: rtl/return_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Add a tiny return-address stack, learned return-PC tags, and one outstanding predicted-return target record with conservative reset/default-not-predict behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Consult the return predictor by current PC, select the RAS top on a learned return-PC hit, and keep EX redirect priority over prediction.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Latch the predicted_return marker through decode while preserving the existing invalid-fetch bubble behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Classify call and return JALR/JAL patterns, train/push/pop the RAS, verify predicted returns against the resolved JALR target, and recover on mismatch.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Preserve current stall and flush priorities while treating redirect as return-misprediction recovery or ordinary unpredicted control flow.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire return predictor lookup, metadata, outstanding-record control, and EX training without changing the nret=1 top-level IO contract.\"\n  - file: test/test_return_predictor.py\n    description: \"Add focused coverage for repeated return prediction, call push behavior, return mismatch recovery, stalls around predicted returns, and reset default-not-predict behavior.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
